WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:01.734
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:02.634
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:04.100
You're here. You made it.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.133
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:06.000
We're in the house.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.801
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:07.801 --> 00:00:09.133
Well, guys,
this is very exciting --

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:12.100
the new movie "The Batman"
has arrived in theaters

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.400
and is expected to make
over $100 million this weekend.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.434
[ Oohs, cheering, and applause ]

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:19.467
So I guess we're cool
with bats again.

00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:22.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:26.334
Yeah, in this movie,
Batman's just psyched

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:28.968
to fight anyone after two years
of "work from cave."

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:31.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:33.601
Did you guys see this?
To celebrate the new movie,

00:00:33.601 --> 00:00:36.100
AMC is selling
a special popcorn bucket

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.534
for just $27.

00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:38.734
Take a look at this thing.

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:41.767
[ Laughter ]
-Aw.

00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:43.367
-I have a feeling
you'll be seeing that taken

00:00:43.367 --> 00:00:45.200
out of someone's house
on the next season

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:46.901
of "Queer Eye." It's like --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.901 --> 00:00:48.067
[ English accent ]
I don't think you need this.

00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:50.801
I think we can remove that.

00:00:50.801 --> 00:00:52.133
I guess it's a cool idea,
though,

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:54.400
but it's still not as fun
as when I saw "Belfast"

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.434
and I ate popcorn
out of Judi Dench's head.

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:59.100
[ Laughter ]
-Aw.
-That was awesome.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.868
It just made you enjoy
the movie that much more, yeah.

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:03.200
Let's get to some news.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.667
Well, we all know that gas
prices have been going up,

00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:07.968
but last night they surged
to the highest point

00:01:07.968 --> 00:01:09.934
in nearly 10 years.

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:11.400
[ Booing ]

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.133
You know it's bad.
Instead of UberPool,

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:14.567
now there's UberPush.

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:16.767
[ Laughter ]
They go, "Where are you from?

00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:18.501
Oh, cool."

00:01:18.501 --> 00:01:19.934
Yeah, gas prices are up,

00:01:19.934 --> 00:01:22.400
which means your coworker
who bikes in every day

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:23.767
just got even more annoying.

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:26.567
[ Laughter ]
"My legs are my gas tank."

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:28.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.334 --> 00:01:29.801
Okay, buddy.
Of course,

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:32.834
gas prices have a lot to do
with what's happening in Ukraine

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:34.133
and, in the face
of growing criticism,

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:36.234
today Vladimir Putin blocked

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:39.033
every Russian citizen
from using Facebook.

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:41.534
-Ew!
-If you think Putin
is unhinged now,

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:42.968
wait 'til nobody remembers
his birthday.

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:45.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:51.033
Yeah, in Russia, the president
has to block Facebook.

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:53.901
Meanwhile, in America, Facebook
has to block the president.

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:55.300
[ Laughter ]
-I think it's very interesting.
-Come on.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:57.601
[ Cheering and applause ]
That works.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.868
Hey, I read that the Space Force
has plans to start

00:02:03.868 --> 00:02:06.601
patrolling the area
around the moon.

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:07.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.834 --> 00:02:09.934
So the Pentagon said
there's a war in Europe

00:02:09.934 --> 00:02:11.701
and the Space Force was like,
"We'll cover the moon."

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:14.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:17.033
Oh, I saw that Disney+
is going to launch

00:02:17.033 --> 00:02:20.868
a cheaper, ad-supported option
on its platform.

00:02:20.868 --> 00:02:23.534
I'm sure kids will be excited
to watch "Encanto" and hear --

00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:24.934
♪ We don't talk about ♪

00:02:24.934 --> 00:02:26.367
Brawny paper towels.

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:29.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:32.767
Meanwhile, Netflix is coming out

00:02:32.767 --> 00:02:37.067
with an interactive daily trivia
series called Trivia Quest.

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:39.667
Sounds fun, until you see
who's asking the questions.

00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:43.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:43.501 --> 00:02:45.667
Some more entertainment news --
NBC just announced

00:02:45.667 --> 00:02:48.534
a new reality show called
"Million Dollar Island,"

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:52.801
where they dump 100 contestants
on an island for 50 days, yeah.

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:54.267
They even have a cool name
for the show --

00:02:54.267 --> 00:02:55.133
"Survivor."

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:59.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:01.434
And, finally, a guy walking
through Times Square

00:03:01.434 --> 00:03:04.167
dropped his wallet
with $4,000 inside,

00:03:04.167 --> 00:03:06.400
then got it all back
after someone found it

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.901
and turned it in to the police.

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:11.267
[ Cheering and applause ]
Yeah.

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:12.067
Yeah.

00:03:15.167 --> 00:03:17.834
Then today, dozens of other
people went to the police like,

00:03:17.834 --> 00:03:19.434
[ Haltingly ]
"I also lost a wallet

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:23.033
[ Laughter ]
with $4,000."

00:03:23.033 --> 00:03:24.367
Police returned
the man's wallet,

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:26.167
then arrested him for whatever
he was planning to do

00:03:26.167 --> 00:03:28.300
[ Laughter ]
in Times Square with $4,000.

